\section{The example of the math formulas}
Please align your math formulas as follows:
\begin{align*}
M^{\pm}(h,\delta)&={\widetilde{M}}^{\pm}(h,\delta)+{g}^{\pm}(0,0,\delta)\int_{L_h^{\pm}}dx-{f}^{\pm}(0,0,\delta)\int_{L_h^{\pm}}dy\\
&=\int_{L_h^{\pm}}{\widetilde{g}}^{\pm}dx-{\widetilde{f}}^{\pm}dy+{g}^{\pm}(0,0,\delta)\int_{L_h^{\pm}}dx-{f}^{\pm}(0,0,\delta)\int_{L_h^{\pm}}dy.
\end{align*}



Here is an example if the math expression exceeds one line:
\begin{align}
{M}(h,\delta)=&2e_1{f}(0,0,\delta)h^{\frac{1}{2}}+\sum\limits_{j\geq2}m_{j-1}(\delta)h^{\frac{j}{2}}+[\varphi(-h^{\frac{j}{2}})-\varphi(h^{\frac{j}{2}})] \notag\\
&+\sum\limits_{j\geq1}((-1)^j-1)e_jh^{\frac{j}{2}} \label{eq1}
\end{align}

For more than one equation:
\begin{align*}
&\widetilde{f}^{\pm}(x,y,\delta)={f}^{\pm}(x,y,\delta)-{f}^{\pm}(0,0,\delta),\\
&\widetilde{g}^{\pm}(x,y,\delta)={g}^{\pm}(x,y,\delta)-{g}^{\pm}(0,0,\delta).
\end{align*}


\section{How to cite theorem, lemma and equation in the paper}

You need to {\bf label} the theorem, lemma and equation of this article first. Then \\

An example of label: ~~~~~~~~~Theorem \ref{th1} is labeled as {\bf th1}. \\

Another example of label: ~~~The equation \eqref{eq1} is labeled as {\bf eq1}.

